From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Agent <claude-agent@invalid>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 10:17:50 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] wayland/color-management: Correct comments on mastering
 primaries

Two comments still said that target volumes are used only for their
peak luminance and that no gamut is mapped with mastering primaries.
Since nativehdr7, declared mastering primaries set the limits of gamut
compression toward an output's declared target gamut. Say so, and why
an extended target volume remains safe to support as declared.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DLZiLBYev72J1s4D37L7Bi
---
 src/wayland/meta-wayland-color-management.c | 18 ++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/wayland/meta-wayland-color-management.c b/src/wayland/meta-wayland-color-management.c
index e7d34e7..1b7d364 100644
--- a/src/wayland/meta-wayland-color-management.c
+++ b/src/wayland/meta-wayland-color-management.c
@@ -1537,10 +1537,15 @@ creator_params_destructor (struct wl_resource *resource)
  *
  * Mastering display primaries are validated the same way. They may lie
  * outside the primary color volume (extended_target_volume is advertised):
- * they are kept and take part in identity, but no gamut is mapped with them,
- * so a target beyond the primary volume cannot cause artifacts. Likewise the
- * mastering luminance may exceed the primary volume's range; only the smaller
- * of the two bounds the content.
+ * they are kept and take part in identity, and when the content can exceed
+ * an output's declared target gamut they set the limits of the gamut
+ * compression toward it (see clutter_color_transform_requires_gamut_compression()).
+ * Content in a bounded encoding is compressed only if its encoding
+ * primaries exceed the target too, and limits from a mastering gamut wider
+ * than the encoding only move colors further inside the target, so a
+ * target beyond the primary volume cannot cause artifacts. Likewise the
+ * mastering luminance may exceed the primary volume's range; only the
+ * smaller of the two bounds the content.
  */
 static gboolean
 creator_params_check_supported (MetaWaylandCreatorParams  *creator_params,
@@ -2389,8 +2394,9 @@ color_manager_send_supported_events (struct wl_resource *resource)
                                               WP_COLOR_MANAGER_V1_FEATURE_SET_LUMINANCES);
   wp_color_manager_v1_send_supported_feature (resource,
                                               WP_COLOR_MANAGER_V1_FEATURE_SET_MASTERING_DISPLAY_PRIMARIES);
-  /* Target volumes are only used for their peak luminance, never to map
-   * gamut, so one exceeding the primary volume is supported as declared. */
+  /* Target volumes give the content's peak luminance and, through
+   * mastering primaries, the limits of gamut compression; both handle a
+   * volume exceeding the primary volume, so one is supported as declared. */
   wp_color_manager_v1_send_supported_feature (resource,
                                               WP_COLOR_MANAGER_V1_FEATURE_EXTENDED_TARGET_VOLUME);
   wp_color_manager_v1_send_supported_tf_named (resource,
